title: The Princess meets to discuss the recent news...
new-page: true

## Unfinished

## You meet with Princess Darlyne in the office (once again idk how many times is it now that you've done this)
## You discuss in detail the announcement of the Supreme Court's Royal Tribunal on the newspaper
## It turns out, the official announcement would be on a speech this afternoon
## Then, you continue to discuss stuff with Princess Darlyne for work
## before leaving to attend the official announcement.

When you enter the Princess's office, you are greeted once more with the sight of Princess Darlyne, sitting on the desk, pouring over a mountain of books and papers.

It's starting to become a rather familiar sight to you nowadays. Rarely, however, is it a good sign. Her overworking herself is almost never a good sign. 

"Good morning, Levon!" Princess Darlyne greets with a wide smile. However, her smile slowly fades into a grimace. "...I suppose you have seen the headline this morning?"

You give a somber nod in reply. Quietly, you note that the circles underneath her eyes have only grown darker since the last time you saw her.

- @where_start: So... where should we even start from? 

@where_start

"So... where should we even start from?" you ask. That question, however, isn't exactly directed towards the Princess — or anyone specific, for that matter. It feels more like throwing a question into the open air and see what answers it will pick up.

Princess Darlyne sighs. It seems certain that she herself doesn't know the answer either.

Frankly, it's hard to come up with any idea on where to start. The tribunal, after all, is a pretty much a can of worms that would need to be unpacked. The prosecution, the defense, the tribunal's judges — heck, those haven't even touched upon whether the tribunal is going to be a fair one in the first place!

So... I suppose

